                <p>I’m interested in the whole system — not just what appears on the screen, but where a request goes, what decides who gets in, and how separate parts become one reliable product.</p>
                <p>That started in high school, when I ran a Minecraft server hosting company for paying customers and learned what breaks when no one is watching. Today it points at the whole of a product: the interface, the service under it, and the deploy that puts it in front of people.</p>
